1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,510
Section 2

2
00:00:01,510 --> 00:00:03,278
Good morning everyone.

3
00:00:03,278 --> 00:00:08,320
My name's Joy Parkins and I'm the restaurant manager.

4
00:00:08,320 --> 00:00:14,410
And I understand that none of you've had any previous experience as kitchen assistants.

5
00:00:14,410 --> 00:00:17,686
Well, you might be feeling a bit nervous now,

6
00:00:17,686 --> 00:00:21,690
but most of our kitchen assistants say they enjoy the work.

7
00:00:21,690 --> 00:00:24,133
OK, they might get shouted at sometimes,

8
00:00:24,133 --> 00:00:25,529
but it's nothing personal,

9
00:00:25,529 --> 00:00:29,716
and they're pleased that they have so many different things to do,

10
00:00:29,716 --> 00:00:31,810
which means they never get bored.

11
00:00:31,810 --> 00:00:38,824
And I'll tell you straightaway that if you do well, we might think about moving you up

12
00:00:38,824 --> 00:00:41,300
and giving you some more responsibility.

13
00:00:41,300 --> 00:00:44,943
Right, well, you've all shown up on time,

14
00:00:44,943 --> 00:00:47,220
which is an excellent start.

15
00:00:47,220 --> 00:00:51,333
Now I'm glad to see none of you have unsuitable footwear,

16
00:00:51,333 --> 00:00:56,942
so that's good - you need to be careful as the floors can get very wet

17
00:00:56,942 --> 00:00:57,690
and slippery.

18
00:00:57,690 --> 00:01:02,426
Those of you with long hair have got it well out of the way,

19
00:01:02,426 --> 00:01:06,824
but some of you'll need to remove your rings and bracelets - just put

20
00:01:06,824 --> 00:01:08,516
them somewhere safe for today,

21
00:01:08,516 --> 00:01:13,252
and remember to leave them at home tomorrow, as they can be a safety

22
00:01:13,252 --> 00:01:13,590
hazard.

23
00:01:13,590 --> 00:01:18,419
Now it's going to be a busy day for you all today - we

24
00:01:18,419 --> 00:01:21,391
don't have any tables free for this evening,

25
00:01:21,391 --> 00:01:23,620
and only a few for lunch.

26
00:01:23,620 --> 00:01:28,402
Fortunately we've got our Head Chef back - he was away on holiday all

27
00:01:28,402 --> 00:01:32,080
last week which meant the other chefs had extra work.

28
00:01:32,080 --> 00:01:37,316
Now, I'll tell you a bit more about the job in a minute

29
00:01:37,316 --> 00:01:39,330
but first, some general regulations.

30
00:01:39,330 --> 00:01:46,050
For all of you, whatever your age, there's some equipment you mustn't use until

31
00:01:46,050 --> 00:01:52,290
you've been properly trained, like the waste disposal system for example, for health

32
00:01:52,290 --> 00:01:53,730
and safety reasons.

33
00:01:53,730 --> 00:01:59,998
Then I think there are two of you here who are under 18 - that's Emma

34
00:01:59,998 --> 00:02:01,670
and Jake, isn't it?

35
00:02:01,670 --> 00:02:01,720
Right.

36
00:02:01,720 --> 00:02:07,360
so for you two, the meat slicer is out of bounds.

37
00:02:07,360 --> 00:02:12,589
And of course none of you are allowed to use the electric mixer until

38
00:02:12,589 --> 00:02:14,830
you've been shown how it works.

39
00:02:14,830 --> 00:02:19,533
Now you may have heard that this can be a stressful job,

40
00:02:19,533 --> 00:02:23,060
and I have to say that can be true.

41
00:02:23,060 --> 00:02:27,868
You'll be working an eight-hour day for the first week, though you'll have the

42
00:02:27,868 --> 00:02:31,990
chance to do overtime after that as well if you want to.

43
00:02:31,990 --> 00:02:37,090
But however long the hours are, you'll get a break in the middle.

44
00:02:37,090 --> 00:02:42,006
What you will find is that you're on your feet all day long, lifting

45
00:02:42,006 --> 00:02:42,708
and carrying,

46
00:02:42,708 --> 00:02:46,220
so if you're not fit now you soon will be!

47
00:02:46,220 --> 00:02:50,783
You'll find you don't have much chance to take it easy - when someone

48
00:02:50,783 --> 00:02:54,644
tells you to do something you need to do it straightaway -

49
00:02:54,644 --> 00:02:59,558
but at least we do have a very efficient air conditioning system compared with

50
00:02:59,558 --> 00:03:00,260
some kitchens.

51
00:03:00,260 --> 00:03:04,470
Now let me tell you about some of the people you need to know.

52
00:03:04,470 --> 00:03:10,732
So as I said, I'm Joy Parkins and I decide who does what during the day

53
00:03:10,732 --> 00:03:13,080
and how long they work for.

54
00:03:13,080 --> 00:03:17,202
I'll be trying to get you to work with as many different people in

55
00:03:17,202 --> 00:03:18,380
the kitchen as possible,

56
00:03:18,380 --> 00:03:21,030
so that you learn while you're on the job.

57
00:03:21,030 --> 00:03:26,520
One person whose name you must remember is David Field.

58
00:03:26,520 --> 00:03:32,451
If you injure yourself at all, even if it's really minor, you must report to him

59
00:03:32,451 --> 00:03:37,640
and he'll make sure the incident is recorded and you get the appropriate treatment.

60
00:03:37,640 --> 00:03:41,040
He's trained to give basic treatment to staff himself,

61
00:03:41,040 --> 00:03:44,440
or he'll send you off somewhere else if necessary.

62
00:03:44,440 --> 00:03:50,616
Then there's Dexter Wills - he's the person you need to see if you smash a plate

63
00:03:50,616 --> 00:03:52,160
or something like that.

64
00:03:52,160 --> 00:03:58,708
Don't just leave it and hope no one will notice - it's really important to get things noted

65
00:03:58,708 --> 00:04:01,790
and replaced or there could be problems later.

66
00:04:01,790 --> 00:04:05,050
And finally, there's Mike Smith.

67
00:04:05,050 --> 00:04:09,978
He's the member of staff who takes care of all the stores of perishables,

68
00:04:09,978 --> 00:04:13,850
so if you notice we're getting low in flour or sugar

69
00:04:13,850 --> 00:04:18,778
or something, make sure you let him know so he can put in an

70
00:04:18,778 --> 00:04:19,130
order.

71
00:04:19,130 --> 00:04:22,390
OK, now the next thing ...
